# YubiKey Management Tools - Agent Context

## Repository Purpose
Collection of shell scripts, GnuPG configuration files, and documentation for managing YubiKeys.
Covers GPG key generation (on-card), PIV-based SSH/VPN keys, git commit signing, U2F/FIDO2, and TOTP.

## Directory Structure
- `gnupg/` - GnuPG configuration files (`gpg.conf`, `gpg-agent.conf`, `scdaemon.conf`, `scd-event`)
- `git/` - Example gitconfig for commit signing
- `piv/` - PIV-specific README
- `scripts/` - Utility shell scripts:
  - `Yubikey-setup.sh` - Full PIV setup (generates SSH + VPN keys, sets PIN/PUK)
  - `Yubikey-piv-reset.sh` - Factory resets the PIV applet
  - `Yubikey-Cert-Import.sh` - Imports a signed VPN certificate
  - `Yubikey-change-pin.sh` - Changes PIV PIN
  - `export-my-key.sh` / `export-others-key.sh` - Export GPG/SSH public keys
  - `print-key-id.sh` - Prints GPG key ID from connected YubiKey
  - `reload-gpg-agent.sh` / `restart-gpg-agent.sh` - Agent management
  - `reset-gpg-applet.sh` - Hard resets the OpenPGP applet (destructive)
- `README.md` - Top-level overview
- `Unix.md` - Detailed setup guide (GPG keys, SSH, git signing, U2F, TOTP, PIV)
- `piv/README.md` - PIV-specific setup with OpenSC

## Key Technical Details
- PIV scripts use `yubico-piv-tool` CLI; GPG scripts use `gpg`, `gpg-connect-agent`, `scdaemon`
- PIV slots: 9a (VPN/authentication), 9e (SSH/card auth)
- GPG SSH support works via `gpg-agent` with `enable-ssh-support`
- Scripts assume macOS primarily; some Linux support (Ubuntu/Debian)
- All Macs are Apple Silicon; Homebrew prefix is `/opt/homebrew/`
- `scd-event` is called by scdaemon on YubiKey insert/removal events
- `gpg-agent.conf` has pinentry-mac enabled for Apple Silicon; Linux pinentry commented out
- `gpg.conf` uses `keys.openpgp.org` keyserver (SKS pool is defunct)
- `scdaemon.conf` uses macOS PCSC framework driver with CCID disabled
- `yubico-piv-tool` must be installed via Homebrew; no bundled binary
- All scripts require their tools to be in PATH

## Completed Maintenance (Feb 2026)
- Replaced defunct SKS keyserver pool with `keys.openpgp.org`
- Removed deprecated `no-honor-keyserver-url` gpg option
- Replaced GNU `getopt --long` in `scd-event` with portable arg parsing (macOS compatible)
- Removed deprecated Slack `files.upload` API calls from `Yubikey-setup.sh`
- Fixed broken line in `export-others-key.sh` (redirect on separate line)
- Fixed sleep/message timing mismatches in reset scripts
- Replaced deprecated `ykpersonalize`/`yubikey-piv-manager` references with `ykman`
- Updated `brew cask install` to `brew install --cask`
- Updated `ykman oath add` to `ykman oath accounts add` (subcommand renamed)
- Removed all Intel Homebrew paths (`/usr/local/`); Apple Silicon only (`/opt/homebrew/`)
- Removed MacGPG2 PATH additions from `scd-event` and `reload-gpg-agent.sh`
- Removed hardcoded `brew --prefix gnupg` from `restart-gpg-agent.sh`
- Activated pinentry-mac for Apple Silicon in `gpg-agent.conf`
- Updated README to document full repo structure including `scripts/` and `piv/`
- Removed bundled yubico-piv-tool v1.5.0 binary; scripts now require it in PATH

## Code Style
- Shell scripts use `#!/bin/bash` or `#!/bin/sh`
- No formal test suite
- Documentation is in Markdown
